json.\n   - A unified Python report (scripts/benchmark_report.py) that reads all results JSON and generates README.md and README.ru.md sections in the exact hierarchy, with tables per size and charts. Update the Python tests; remove or replace rust/out.py and csharp/out.py.\n   - Workflows: a benchmarks matrix plus a report-and-commit job; rust.yml and CI.yml for build, test and smoke; update dependabot (add cargo); consider removing the legacy cpp.yml.\n   - Measure throughput locally to choose sizes, W (constant total work) and the job split; document the choices in the PR.\n   - Commit atomically, push, verify CI, update PR #108 title and description, then run `gh pr ready 108`.\n\n8. **Current work**\n   - Researching APIs to design the symmetric implementation.\n   - The last action was grepping for `Itself` handling. The result: the C# memory Update has no Itself translation (only `EnsureLinkIsItselfOrExists` in the extensions), and the Rust store has none either. So markers and posts must be created explicitly as `create()` followed by `update(m, root_or_marker, m)`.\n   - No code has been written yet.\n\n9. **Next step**\n   - Start implementing the Rust rewrite in rust/:\n     - New Cargo.toml (stable, edition 2024, doublets 0.5.0, platform-data 2.0.0, rusqlite 0.40.2 bundled).\n     - Generic `T: LinkReference` links storage trait with SQLite and Doublets implementations.\n     - The dataset with `from(i) = 1 + splitmix64(2i) % i`, `to(i) = i + 1 − from(i)`, and the stride permutation.\n     - The lifecycle harness writing JSON.\n   - Then quickly verify that `LinksConstants::external()` with raw-number symbols works in doublets-rs.\n   - Then measure throughput at 100k, 1M and 10M (in ./experiments) to choose the size and repetition schedule and the CI job split.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-