[2026-10-04T17:01:25.789Z] [INFO]         "thinking": "I've confirmed the root cause: in doublets 0.5.0, `split::Store::update_links` checks virtuality after detaching the link, so a self-referencing update incorrectly registers as unused and gets routed to the external tree, causing a later panic on delete. The duplicate-link issue I saw earlier was my own test error, not an actual bug—C#'s equivalent avoids this by checking `ExternalReferencesRange` instead.\n\n",
