[2026-10-04T17:41:27.680Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n   - Draft PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n   - When finishing:\n     - Merge main if needed.\n     - Make sure CI passes.\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments.\n     - Update the PR description in the style of merged PR #106.\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples.\n   - Git user is konard.\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user, such as for authorship or attribution. It must never be sent to an unrelated service (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - **Issue #107 requirements:**\n     - README results generated in exactly this hierarchy:\n       ```\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for links\n         Rust doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit address/id space benchmarks\n           64 bit address/id space benchmarks\n         C# doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit\n           64 bit\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for objects\n         (same structure)\n       ```\n     - SQLite table `links(id, from, to)` with the obvious indices, and the same id type in C# and Rust.\n     - Fully symmetrical coverage.\n     - Object benchmarks with and without a sequences cache, in all languages.\n     - Latest versions of all dependencies.\n     - Short, self-explanatory code.\n     - No false positives or false negatives.\n     - The largest sizes that fit within the 6-hour CI limit (100k, 1M, 10M, 100M), splitting CI jobs if needed.\n     - Fewer repetitions at large sizes and more at 100k, \"but not too much\".\n     - Follow best practices.\n     - \"Make it perfect, please.\"\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Rust**\n     - doublets 0.5.0 and rusqlite 0.40.2 (bundled).\n     - Split store bug in doublets 0.5.0: updating a link so it references itself corrupts the store. Workaround: update it to (0, 0) first. Documented in experiments/split_store_delete.\n   - **C# setup**\n     - net10.0 with Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12 (bundles SQLite 3.53.3).\n     - Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1 and Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences 0.6.5.\n   - **C# delete root cause**\n     - `links.Delete(id)` binds to the Platform.Data extension, which is a raw delete. It frees the link without detaching it from the source and target trees.\n     - Stale entries then hide other links from `SearchOrDefault`, especially when self-referencing links exist.\n     - The correct call is the Platform.Data.Doublets overload `links.Delete(id, handler: null)`, which calls EnforceResetValues (updates the link to (0, 0)) before deleting.\n     - The legacy repo code avoided this by calling `Platform.Data.ILinksExtensions.Delete`... In fact it is unclear which overload the legacy code bound to.\n   - **C# split store and raw numbers**\n     - Objects store raw numbers (via AddressToRawNumberConverter) as link sources, for example the Unicode symbols.\n     - The split store needs `new LinksConstants<T>(enableExternalReferencesSupport: true)`. Otherwise it throws AccessViolationException in InternalLinksSourcesLinkedListMethods.GetLast.\n     - The legacy DoubletsDbContext created these constants but never passed them to the store.\n     - Constructors that take constants:\n       - `UnitedMemoryLinks<T>(memory, UnitedMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, constants, IndexTreeType.Default)`\n       - `SplitMemoryLinks<T>(data, index, SplitMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, constants)`\n   - **Rust constants**\n     - Rust's default `LinksConstants::new()` is internal-only.\n     - Objects stores now use `with_constants(..., LinksConstants::external())`, for symmetry with C#. This works and the Rust tests pass.\n   - **Links stores** use the default (internal-only) constants in both languages.\n   - **Microsoft.Data.Sqlite transactions:** every command's Transaction must be set during the transaction and reset to null afterwards.\n   - **xunit v3 4.0.1 on the .NET 10 SDK** needs Microsoft.Testing.Platform, configured in global.json with `\"test\": {\"runner\": \"Microsoft.Testing.Platform\"}`, and run with `dotnet test --project SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests`. Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk and xunit.runner.visualstudio were removed.\n   - **Repetitions:** `clamp(work / size, 1, 10)` with a default work of 3M in both languages. This gives 100k → 10, 1M → 3, 10M → 1.\n   - **Sizing (local machine: 6 CPUs, 11 GB RAM)**\n     - Rust links, 64-bit:\n       - 100k: about 16 s per repetition for all variants.\n       - 1M: about 298 s per repetition.\n       - 10M: estimated at 1–1.5 h.\n       - 100M is excluded (over 6 h, plus memory and disk).\n     - Rust objects, 64-bit:\n       - 100k: 134 s for one repetition of all 10 variants.\n       - The uncached Doublets variants dominate: create takes about 100–160 µs/op.\n       - Split_NonVolatile_Uncached delete takes 113 µs/op.\n       - Planned objects sizes: 10k, 100k and 1M.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n   - **Commit 29ec139 \"Rewrite C# benchmarks on net10.0 with the same lifecycle as Rust\"**\n     - Deletes the legacy C# files.\n     - Adds csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/ containing: SQLiteVSDoublets.csproj, Dataset.cs, SQLiteStorage.cs, Links.cs, Objects.cs, Harness.cs and Program.cs.\n     - Adds csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests/ and csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets.slnx.\n     - Updates csharp/global.json and the root .gitignore (adds `bin/` and `obj/`).\n   - **SQLiteStorage.cs** — Transaction now resets the commands:\n     ```csharp\n     using var transaction = _connection.BeginTransaction();\n     _commands.ForEach(command => command.Transaction = transaction);\n     try { var result = work(); transaction.Commit(); return result; }\n     finally { _commands.ForEach(command => command.Transaction = null); }\n     ```\n   - **Links.cs** — DoubletsLinks: `public void Delete(T id) => links.Delete(id, handler: null);`\n   - **Objects.cs** — DoubletsBlogPosts.Delete:\n     ```csharp\n     var objectProperty = _links.SearchOrDefault(id, property);\n     _links.Delete(_links.SingleOrDefault([_any, objectProperty, _any])![0], handler: null);\n     _links.Delete(objectProperty, handler: null);\n     ...\n     _links.Delete(id, handler: null);\n     ```\n   - **Harness.cs**\n     - Adds `using Platform.Data;` and `using Platform.Data.Doublets.Memory;`.\n     - The United and Split helpers are now public:\n       ```csharp\n       /// <summary>Objects store numbers and Unicode symbols as raw numbers, which are external references.\n       public static ILinks<T> United<T>(IResizableDirectMemory memory, bool external = false) ... =>\n           new UnitedMemoryLinks<T>(memory, UnitedMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, new LinksConstants<T>(external), IndexTreeType.Default);\n       public static ILinks<T> Split<T>(IResizableDirectMemory data, IResizableDirectMemory index, bool external = false) ... =>\n           new SplitMemoryLinks<T>(data, index, SplitMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, new LinksConstants<T>(external));\n       ```\n     - MeasureObjects passes `external: true` to all four Doublets factories.\n   - **csharp/global.json:** sdk 10.0.100 (latestFeature, no prerelease), plus `\"test\": {\"runner\": \"Microsoft.Testing.Platform\"}`.\n   - **SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests.csproj**\n     - net10.0, ImplicitUsings, Nullable, TreatWarningsAsErrors, OutputType Exe.\n     - ProjectReference to the main project; PackageReference xunit.v3 4.0.1.\n   - **SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests/StoragesTests.cs** mirrors the Rust tests. All 28 tests pass in about 22 s:\n     - LinksAreUniqueAndReferenceCreatedIds.\n     - ScatteredVisitsEveryIdOnce (theory over 1, 2, 3, 10, 1000, 1024 and 65536).\n     - EveryLinksVariantPassesTheLifecycle and EveryObjectsVariantPassesTheLifecycle, as MemberData theories over Harness.LinksVariants and ObjectsVariants, for uint and ulong.\n     - SplitStoreKeepsLinksUpdatedToReferenceThemselves.\n     - LifecycleRejectsAStorageThatLosesRecords: a Lossy wrapper whose Each = EachWithFrom(1); expects InvalidOperationException starting with \"query_all returned unexpected records\".\n     - EveryObjectsStorageReturnsTheStoredPosts (theory over cached false/true):\n       - RoundTrip covers 20 posts plus `(\"Ünïcödé 🌍 ✓\",\"a\",0)` and `(\"\",\"ab\",uint.MaxValue/2)`.\n       - Checks Get, Each (sorted by id), then deletes everything and checks Count is 0.\n       - Uses `Harness.United/Split(..., external: true)`.\n   - **Commit 4f8d0c5 \"Rust: external references for objects stores, clamp repetitions to 1..=10\"**\n     - rust/src/harness.rs:\n       - Imports `data::{LinkReference, LinksConstants}`.\n       - In measure_objects, uses `unit::Store::<T,_>::with_constants(mem, LinksConstants::external())` and `split::Store::<T,_,_>::with_constants(data, index, LinksConstants::external())`.\n     - rust/tests/storages.rs: round_trip uses the same with_constants calls.\n     - rust/src/main.rs:\n       - `const DEFAULT_WORK: u64 = 3_000_000; const MAX_REPETITIONS: u64 = 10;`\n       - Computes `(work / size).clamp(1, MAX_REPETITIONS)`.\n       - Updated the doc comment.\n     - Also adds experiments/sizing/run.sh.\n     - cargo fmt, clippy `-D warnings` and `cargo test --release` (7 tests) all pass.\n   - **Uncommitted: experiments/csharp_tree_delete/** (csharp_tree_delete.csproj references ../../csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets; Program.cs)\n     - Header comment explains why the benchmarks use `Platform.Data.Doublets.ILinksExtensions.Delete(links, id, handler)`.\n     - Supports `--self` (also creates self-referencing links) and `--reset` (uses the resetting delete).\n     - Searches n from 2 to 300 for the first failure in the united and split stores.\n     - Results so far:\n       - With `--self` and the raw delete:\n         - United fails at 9 links, e.g. \"after deleting 8 search(5, 5) = 0 instead of 6\".\n         - Split fails at 3 links: (1: 1 1) (2: 2 1) (3: 3 1); after deleting 3, search(1, 1) = 0.\n       - With no flags (no self-references, raw delete): no failure seen before the run was stopped.\n       - The `--reset` run (and `--self --reset`) is still in background task btbekhxdq.\n     - experiments/csharp_object_delete was removed (superseded).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **Stale transaction error:** \"The transaction object is not associated with the same connection object\". Fixed by resetting Transaction to null in a finally block.\n   - **NullReferenceException in DoubletsBlogPosts.Delete:** the root cause was the raw Platform.Data delete corrupting the trees, so `SearchOrDefault(8, 5)` returned 0 after (8, 4) was deleted. Fixed with `Delete(id, handler: null)`.\n   - **AccessViolationException in split objects:** caused by raw-number sources without external-reference constants. Fixed by passing `LinksConstants<T>(true)`.\n   - **VSTest not supported on the .NET 10 SDK:** fixed by switching to MTP in global.json and removing the VSTest packages.\n   - **Exit 144 after `pkill -f csharp_tree_delete`:** the command killed its own shell. Kill by pid via pgrep on the \"bin/Debug/net10.0/csharp_tree\" path instead.\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - The C# CLI smoke run passes in Release for links 1000 and objects 100 at 32 and 64 bits, with sqlite_version 3.53.3. Output files: /tmp/cs-{links,objects}-{32,64}.json.\n   - All C# tests and Rust tests pass.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 / Your prepared branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/pull/108 / Proceed.\"\n   - Security constraint (from context): the email link.assistant.team@proton.me is for identification only (authorship or attribution). Never send it to unrelated services unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - Periodic system prompts: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\"\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - Wait for, or check, the background `--reset` experiment output (/tmp/claude-1001/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1791131286882/78aa02d9-2054-4be5-9990-31ae739e08df/tasks/btbekhxdq.output), then commit experiments/csharp_tree_delete.\n   - Run C# sizing at 100k and 1M (links and objects, Release build) to compare with Rust, and finalize sizes:\n     - Links: 100k, 1M, 10M.\n     - Objects: 10k, 100k, 1M.\n     - 100M excluded and documented, possibly behind a workflow_dispatch `sizes` input.\n   - Write a unified Python report (scripts/benchmark_report.py with tests) that turns results/*.json into README.md and README.ru.md sections in the required hierarchy, with charts in docs/benchmarks. Remove references to the deleted csharp/out.py.\n   - Workflows:\n     - A benchmark matrix (language × bits × category × size, each job ≤ 6 h) plus a report/commit job.\n     - Rewrite rust.yml (fmt, clippy, test, smoke).\n     - Rewrite CI.yml for net10.0 (build, `dotnet test --project`, smoke); it currently references the removed --self-test and out.py.\n     - Add cargo to dependabot; consider removing cpp.yml.\n   - Document the bugs: the doublets-rs split self-reference bug, the C# delete overload, and the external-references requirement. Also document the sizes and the exclusion of 100M.\n   - Push, check CI, update PR #108's title and description, then run `gh pr ready 108`.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n   - Planning the CI matrix and sizes from sizing data.\n   - The last step was reviewing /tmp/sizing-objects100k.out: Rust objects 64-bit at 100k took 134 s for one repetition of all variants.\n   - Both commits (29ec139 and 4f8d0c5) are local and not pushed yet.\n   - The only uncommitted item is experiments/csharp_tree_delete/.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n   - Check the btbekhxdq output and commit experiments/csharp_tree_delete.\n   - Push the branch.\n   - Run C# Release sizing for links (100k) and objects (100k), with one repetition each, for example:\n     ```\n     dotnet csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/bin/Release/net10.0/sqlite-vs-doublets.dll links 64 100000 --repetitions 1 --directory /tmp/cs-sizing --output /tmp/cs-sizing-links-64-100000.json\n     ```\n   - Then design the benchmark workflow matrix and the report script.\n</summary>\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1791131286882/78aa02d9-2054-4be5-9990-31ae739e08df.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
