[2026-10-04T18:06:19.270Z] [INFO]       {
[2026-10-04T18:06:19.270Z] [INFO]         "type": "text",
[2026-10-04T18:06:19.270Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n   - Draft PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n   - When finishing:\n     - Merge main if needed.\n     - Make sure CI passes.\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments.\n     - Update the PR description in the style of merged PR #106.\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples.\n   - Git user is konard.\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user, such as for authorship or attribution. It must never be sent to an unrelated service (request header, URL or payload) unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - **Issue #107 requirements:**\n     - README results generated in exactly this hierarchy:\n       ```\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for links\n         Rust doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit address/id space benchmarks\n           64 bit address/id space benchmarks\n         C# doublets vs SQLite\n           32 bit\n           64 bit\n       Doublets vs SQLite as storage for objects\n         (same structure)\n       ```\n     - SQLite table `links(id, from, to)` with the obvious indices, and the same id type in C# and Rust.\n     - Fully symmetrical coverage.\n     - Object benchmarks with and without a sequences cache, in all languages.\n     - Latest versions of all dependencies.\n     - Short, self-explanatory code.\n     - No false positives or false negatives.\n     - The largest sizes that fit within the 6-hour CI limit (100k, 1M, 10M, 100M), splitting CI jobs if needed.\n     - Fewer repetitions at large sizes and more at 100k, \"but not too much\".\n     - Follow best practices.\n     - \"Make it perfect, please.\"\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Rust**\n     - doublets 0.5.0 and rusqlite 0.40.2 (bundled SQLite 3.53.2).\n     - Split store self-reference bug, worked around by updating to (0, 0) first. Documented in experiments/split_store_delete.\n     - Objects stores use `with_constants(..., LinksConstants::external())`.\n   - **C# setup**\n     - net10.0 with Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12 (SQLite 3.53.3).\n     - Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1 and Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences 0.6.5.\n     - Platform.Data's `ReadHandler` and `WriteHandler` live in the `Platform.Delegates` namespace.\n   - **C# delete:** `links.Delete(id, handler: null)` (the resetting Platform.Data.Doublets overload) is required. The raw Platform.Data delete corrupts the trees.\n   - **C# objects:** need `new LinksConstants<T>(true)` (external references) for both United and Split.\n   - **New finding: C# UnitedMemoryLinks trees degenerate in the objects workload.**\n     - Affected tree types: Default, SizeBalancedTree and RecursionlessSizeBalancedTree.\n     - Cause: the AttachCore recursion becomes O(n) deep, so create is O(n) per post.\n     - `IndexTreeType.SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree` fixes it: 4.3 µs versus 677 µs per hub update at 10k posts.\n     - The enum values are Default, SizeBalancedTree, RecursionlessSizeBalancedTree and SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree.\n   - **Repetitions:** clamp(3M / size, 1, 10) in both languages.\n   - **Sizing (local machine)**\n     - Rust links, 64-bit: 100k is about 16 s per repetition for all variants; 1M is about 298 s.\n     - C# links, 64-bit, 100k: 24.7 s total.\n     - Rust objects, 64-bit, 100k: 134 s per repetition for all variants.\n     - C# objects: United degenerates (see above).\n   - **Doublets file sizes:** these are the preallocated mmap size (64 MiB for united, 80 MiB for split). This must be documented in the README legend.\n   - **Planned CI design**\n     - One job per (language, category, bits, size), all variants on the same runner, so comparisons inside a table are valid.\n     - Sizes: links 100k, 1M, 10M; objects 100k, 1M. 100M is excluded because it exceeds 6 h, especially for SQLite update and delete.\n     - About 20 jobs in total.\n     - Results JSON is stamped with run_url, date and machine via jq, then committed to docs/benchmarks/results/.\n     - A report job (`if: always() && !cancelled()`) generates README sections and charts and commits them to the triggering branch.\n     - PRs run a smoke-size validation.\n     - Possibly add a temporary push trigger on the PR branch so the PR shows real results, then remove it.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Harness.cs** (committed in 29ec139; needs a change)\n     - The United helper currently uses IndexTreeType.Default:\n       ```csharp\n       public static ILinks<T> United<T>(IResizableDirectMemory memory, bool external = false) where T : struct, IBinaryInteger<T>, IUnsignedNumber<T>, IMinMaxValue<T> =>\n           new UnitedMemoryLinks<T>(memory, UnitedMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, new LinksConstants<T>(external), IndexTreeType.Default);\n       public static ILinks<T> Split<T>(IResizableDirectMemory data, IResizableDirectMemory index, bool external = false) ... =>\n           new SplitMemoryLinks<T>(data, index, SplitMemoryLinks<T>.DefaultLinksSizeStep, new LinksConstants<T>(external));\n       ```\n     - It also contains the LinksVariants and ObjectsVariants arrays, WarmUpSize = 10_000, Tally, LinksLifecycle, ObjectsLifecycle, Measurement.ToJson (median_ns, min_ns, max_ns, samples_ns), Measure, MeasureLinks and MeasureObjects.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Objects.cs**\n     - DoubletsBlogPosts uses PropertiesOperator, StringToUnicodeSequenceConverter with BalancedVariantConverter, and CachingConverterDecorator when cached.\n     - Delete uses `handler: null`.\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Links.cs**\n     - SQLiteLinks has the table `links (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"from\", \"to\")` and the indexes links_from_to and links_to_from.\n     - DoubletsLinks uses `links.Delete(id, handler: null)`.\n   - **scripts/benchmark_report.py** (rewritten, not committed)\n     - Usage: `benchmark_report.py RESULTS_DIR [--readme README.md] [--readme README.ru.md] [--charts DIR]`.\n     - Markers: `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_START-->` and `<!--BENCHMARK_RESULTS_END-->`.\n     - Constants: CATEGORIES = (\"links\", \"objects\"), LANGUAGES = (\"Rust\", \"C#\"), BITS = (32, 64).\n     - OPERATIONS:\n       - Links: create, query_all, query_by_id, query_by_from_to, query_by_from, query_by_to, update, delete.\n       - Objects: create, read_all, read_by_id, delete.\n     - TEXT contains en and ru dictionaries with these keys: category headings, `language`, `bits`, `size`, `operations` labels, `storage`, `file_size`, `faster`, `slower`, `same`, `provenance`, `repetitions`, `machine`, `local`, `run`, `missing`, `chart` and `nouns`.\n       - `repetitions` is a lambda; the Russian version uses `russian_plural(count, one, few, many)`.\n     - Functions:\n       - `load(dir)` returns reports keyed by (category, language, bits, size) and raises on duplicates.\n       - `baseline(variant)` maps NonVolatile to SQLite_File and other Doublets variants to SQLite_Memory.\n       - `duration(ns)` formats with 3 significant digits in s, ms, µs or ns.\n       - `size(count)` formats with thousands separators.\n       - `file_size(bytes)` returns MiB, or \"—\" when the value is None.\n       - `comparison(measured, reference, text)` returns \"≈ same\" when the min–max ranges overlap, otherwise \"N× faster\" or \"N× slower\".\n       - `table(report, text)` has rows for variants and columns for operations plus File size.\n       - `provenance(report, text)` uses report.get(\"run_url\"), \"date\" and \"machine\".\n       - `chart_name(category, language, bits)` returns `{category}-{rust|csharp}-{bits}.png`.\n       - `section(reports, language_code, charts_link)` writes `##`/`###`/`####`/`#####` headings. Missing groups show \"_No results yet._\".\n       - `replace_section(document, generated)`.\n       - `charts(reports, directory)` draws one log-scale grouped bar figure per (category, language, bits), with one subplot per size, saved at dpi 80.\n       - `main()` uses the Russian text for any README whose name ends with `.ru.md`.\n     - Verified on a sample in /tmp/report-test; the output renders correctly.\n   - **scripts/test_benchmark_report.py:** the old version must be rewritten for the new script.\n   - **experiments/csharp_tree_delete/** (uncommitted)\n     - Program.cs has `--self` and `--reset` flags and now uses `Enumerable.Range(2, 150)`.\n     - Results:\n       - With `--self` and the raw delete: United fails at 9 links and Split fails at 3 links.\n       - The `--reset` result is pending, in /tmp/tree-reset.log.\n   - **experiments/csharp_objects_profile/** (uncommitted)\n     - Program.cs wraps ILinks in a `Profiled` decorator that counts and times Count, Each (by restriction shape), Create, Update (by source/target kind: raw, markerN or link) and Delete.\n     - Usage: `<united|split> <n> [IndexTreeType]`.\n     - It references Harness and DoubletsBlogPosts from the main project.\n     - csproj: net10.0 with a ProjectReference to ../../csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets.\n   - **experiments/csharp_united_hub/** (uncommitted): measures hub attach scaling. It showed no degradation for simple hubs.\n   - **Workflows (to rewrite)**\n     - CI.yml (C#) still references net8.0, `--self-test` and out.py.\n     - rust.yml uses nightly-2022-08-22, criterion and out.py.\n     - cpp.yml is legacy.\n     - dependabot.yml covers nuget only; cargo needs adding.\n   - **README.md and README.ru.md**\n     - Old sections with CSHARP_/RUST_ markers and stale local-run instructions need replacing with a single marker pair.\n     - Add methodology prose, local run instructions, sizes and the reason 100M is excluded, and the known bugs.\n     - The historical C# results sections can stay.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **Earlier session errors**\n     - Stale transaction: fixed by resetting command.Transaction in a finally block.\n     - NullReferenceException on delete: fixed with `Delete(id, handler: null)`.\n     - AccessViolationException in split objects: fixed with external-reference constants.\n     - VSTest not supported on the .NET 10 SDK: fixed with MTP in global.json.\n   - **Exit 144:** caused by pkill/pgrep `-f` matching the agent's own shell. Fixed by running the sampling from a script file (/tmp/sample_stacks.sh) that uses `$!`.\n   - **Experiment build error:** `ReadHandler`/`WriteHandler` were not found. Fixed with `using Platform.Delegates;`.\n   - **matplotlib missing locally:** installed version 3.11.2 with pip.\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - The C# objects quadratic slowdown is root-caused to UnitedMemoryLinks size-balanced tree degeneration. The fix is SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree, which still needs to be applied and verified.\n   - Rust objects 64-bit results (median ns/op):\n\n     At 10k:\n\n     | Variant | create | delete | read_all | read_by_id |\n     |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n     | SQLite_Memory | 1867 | 4225 | — | — |\n     | Doublets_United_Volatile_Cached | 8203 | — | — | — |\n     | Doublets_United_Volatile_Uncached | 150005 | — | — | — |\n\n     At 100k:\n\n     | Variant | create | delete | read_all | read_by_id |\n     |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n     | SQLite_Memory | 2842 | 5178 | 1203 | 3609 |\n     | SQLite_File | 4775 | 23298 | — | — |\n     | Doublets_United_Volatile_Cached | 12416 | 25166 | — | — |\n     | Doublets_United_*_Uncached | about 150000 | — | — | — |\n     | Doublets_Split_NonVolatile_Uncached | — | 113772 | — | — |\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 / Your prepared branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/pull/108 / Proceed.\"\n   - Security constraint (from context): the email link.assistant.team@proton.me is for identification only (authorship or attribution). Never send it to unrelated services unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - Periodic system prompts: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\"\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - Apply IndexTreeType.SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree to the C# United helper in Harness.cs.\n     - Decide whether to apply it to links too; preferably all United stores, for consistency.\n     - Rerun the C# tests (`dotnet test --project SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests` from csharp/) and the C# objects sizing at 100k (and at 1M if feasible).\n     - Kill the stale background objects sizing process (task b04geyo9u, pid 66858) first.\n   - Document the tree degeneration in experiments/csharp_objects_profile (add a header comment with the measured numbers), plus csharp_united_hub if kept.\n     - Commit the experiments, including csharp_tree_delete once the `--reset` results arrive (/tmp/tree-reset.log).\n   - Rewrite scripts/test_benchmark_report.py (unittest) for the new report script.\n     - Add scripts/requirements.txt pinning matplotlib==3.11.2.\n     - Commit.\n   - Workflows:\n     - New benchmarks workflow: a matrix plus a report/commit job, a PR smoke run, and push to main plus workflow_dispatch triggers. Consider a temporary branch trigger to produce real results for the PR.\n     - Rewrite rust.yml: stable toolchain, fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, `cargo test --release`, smoke run.\n     - Rewrite CI.yml for .NET 10: build with warnings as errors, `dotnet test --project SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests`, smoke run.\n     - Add cargo to dependabot (directory /rust), plus github-actions.\n     - Consider removing cpp.yml.\n   - Update README.md and README.ru.md:\n     - A single marker section.\n     - Methodology and legend: same-durability baselines, \"≈ same\" meaning overlapping ranges, Doublets file sizes being the preallocated mmap.\n     - Run instructions, sizes and the 100M exclusion.\n     - Known bugs: the doublets-rs split self-reference bug, the C# delete overload, the external references requirement and the united SBT degeneration.\n     - Remove the stale old result sections and charts (docs/benchmarks/bench_*.png).\n   - Push, check CI (download logs on failure), update PR #108's title and description, then run `gh pr ready 108`.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n   - Investigating the slow C# objects benchmark. The last experiment ran:\n     ```\n     for t in Default SizeBalancedTree RecursionlessSizeBalancedTree SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree; do ... csharp_objects_profile.dll united 10000 $t ...\n     ```\n   - Its result: only SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree stays fast. For posts 9001..10000, Update[marker7,link] cost 4286 ns, versus 677509 ns with Default.\n   - Background processes possibly still running:\n     - The C# objects sizing at 100k (task b04geyo9u, writing to /tmp/cs-sizing-objects.log).\n     - The csharp_tree_delete `--reset` run (task bywppjwpu, writing to /tmp/tree-reset.log).\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n   - Change the `United<T>` helper in csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Harness.cs to pass `IndexTreeType.SizedAndThreadedAVLBalancedTree`, with a doc comment explaining why: the size-balanced trees degenerate when many links attach to the same marker, as measured in experiments/csharp_objects_profile.\n   - Run the C# tests.\n   - Kill the old sizing process and rerun `dotnet SQLiteVSDoublets/bin/Release/net10.0/sqlite-vs-doublets.dll objects 64 100000 --r