[2026-10-04T18:20:06.832Z] [INFO]         "content": "1\t[![Actions Status](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/workflows/CI/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions?workflow=CI)\n2\t\n3\t# Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets ([русская версия](README.ru.md))\n4\t\n5\t![Comparison of models](https://github.com/LinksPlatform/Documentation/raw/master/doc/ModelsComparison/relational_model_vs_associative_model_vs_links.png)\n6\t\n7\tComparison of SQLite and LinksPlatform's Doublets (links) on basic embedded database operations with links and object-like structures.\n8\t\n9\tBased on examples from https://github.com/FahaoTang/dotnetcore-examples and https://github.com/Konard/LinksPlatform\n10\t\n11\t## Automated benchmark suite\n12\t\n13\tThe comparison runs the same link workload against SQLite in-memory and file\n14\tdatabases and four Doublets layouts: united/split and volatile/non-volatile.\n15\tIt measures create, update, delete, enumerate all, and queries by identity,\n16\tconcrete `(source, target)`, outgoing source, and incoming target. The Rust\n17\tsuite also measures creation, reading, and deletion of object-like blog posts\n18\ton every storage variant.\n19\t\n20\tPreparation and cleanup are outside the measured region. Pull requests run a\n21\treduced-scale validation and preserve raw output, tables, and charts as\n22\tworkflow artifacts. Full runs on `main` publish the tables and charts below\n23\twith a link to the producing workflow run.\n24\t\n25\tRun the checks locally:\n26\t\n27\t```bash\n28\tcd rust\n29\tcargo test --lib --tests\n30\tcargo check --benches\n31\tBENCHMARK_LINK_COUNT=10 BACKGROUND_LINK_COUNT=30 \\\n32\t  BENCHMARK_OBJECT_COUNT=5 cargo bench --bench bench -- \\\n33\t  --output-format bencher\n34\t\n35\tcd ../csharp\n36\tdotnet run -c Release -- --self-test\n37\tBENCHMARK_LINK_COUNT=10 BACKGROUND_LINK_COUNT=30 \\\n38\t  dotnet run -c Release -- --filter '*LinksBenchmarks*'\n39\t```