[2026-10-04T18:22:25.880Z] [INFO]                 "+- In C#, links are deleted with `Delete(id, handler: null)`, which resets the link before deleting it; the bare `Delete(id)` leaves the link in the index trees, and later searches fail ([experiments/csharp_tree_delete](experiments/csharp_tree_delete)).",
[2026-10-04T18:22:25.880Z] [INFO]                 "+- The C# united stores use AVL index trees: the default size balanced trees degenerate when many links share a source or a target, which makes each blog post creation linear in the number of posts ([experiments/csharp_objects_profile](experiments/csharp_objects_profile)).",
[2026-10-04T18:22:25.880Z] [INFO]                 "+- Objects stores use external references for numbers and Unicode symbols, so raw values never collide with link ids.",
[2026-10-04T18:22:25.880Z] [INFO]                 "+- Reading a string without the cache walks its sequence link by link; in C# each `GetSource`/`GetTarget` call of `Platform.Data` allocates a handler and a list, which makes the uncached C# reads much slower than the Rust ones.",
