[2026-10-04T19:20:46.854Z] [INFO]         "content": " .github/dependabot.yml                             |  11 +-\n .github/workflows/CI.yml                           | 198 ------\n .github/workflows/benchmarks.yml                   | 130 ++++\n .github/workflows/csharp.yml                       |  33 +\n .github/workflows/rust.yml                         | 224 +------\n .gitignore                                         |   7 +\n README.md                                          | 140 ++--\n README.ru.md                                       | 140 ++--\n csharp/Benchmarks.cs                               |  55 --\n csharp/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets.csproj         |  34 -\n csharp/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets.sln            |  25 -\n csharp/Doublets/DoubletsDbContext.cs               | 414 ------------\n csharp/Doublets/DoubletsTestRun.cs                 | 117 ----\n csharp/Links/DoubletsLinksStorage.cs               |  78 ---\n csharp/Links/ILinksStorage.cs                      |  27 -\n csharp/Links/LinkRecord.cs                         |   3 -\n csharp/Links/LinksData.cs                          |  38 --\n csharp/Links/LinksStorageFactory.cs                |  55 --\n csharp/Links/SQLiteLinksStorage.cs                 | 150 -----\n csharp/LinksBenchmarks.cs                          | 149 -----\n csharp/LinksSelfTest.cs                            |  58 --\n csharp/Model/BlogPost.cs                           |  62 --\n csharp/Model/BlogPosts.cs                          |  68 --\n csharp/Program.cs                                  | 101 ---\n csharp/SQLite/SQLiteDbContext.cs                   |  85 ---\n csharp/SQLite/SQLiteTestRun.cs                     |  81 ---\n .../SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests.csproj                  |  20 +\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets.Tests/StoragesTests.cs     | 111 ++++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets.slnx                       |   4 +\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Dataset.cs                 | 119 ++++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Harness.cs                 | 347 ++++++++++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Links.cs                   | 134 ++++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Objects.cs                 | 189 ++++++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Program.cs                 |  62 ++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/SQLiteStorage.cs           |  62 ++\n csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/SQLiteVSDoublets.csproj    |  20 +\n csharp/SizeAfterCreationColumn.cs                  | 194 ------\n csharp/TestRun.cs                                  | 137 ----\n csharp/TestRunResults.cs                           | 119 ----\n csharp/global.json                                 |   5 +-\n== 229ae26\nRewrite Rust benchmarks on stable doublets 0.5.0 and rusqlite 0.40\n\n- One CLI runs links or objects benchmarks for 32 or 64 bit ids at any size\n- SQLite stores links(id, from, to) with (from, to) and (to, from) indexes\n- Doublets objects mirror Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences, with and without a sequences cache\n- Every timed batch is validated by count and order-sensitive checksum\n- Work around a doublets 0.5.0 split store bug with links updated to reference themselves\n\n== 29ec139\nRewrite C# benchmarks on net10.0 with the same lifecycle as Rust\n\nReplace the legacy BenchmarkDotNet project with a small CLI and an xunit v3 test\nproject. Both languages now share the dataset, the validated lifecycle, the\nvariant names and the JSON results format, for 32 and 64 bit ids.\n\nDoublets links are deleted with the Platform.Data.Doublets overload that resets\nthem first, and objects stores enable external references for raw numbers.\n\n== 4f8d0c5\nRust: external references for objects stores, clamp repetitions to 1..=10\n\nRaw numbers stored by the objects layout are external references, as in C#.\nRepetitions default to 3M / size clamped to 1..=10 in both languages, and\nexperiments/sizing times one repetition of each variant to plan CI jobs.\n\n== ab53110\nC#: AVL index trees for the united store; delete and tree experiments\n\nThe united store's size balanced trees degenerate in the objects workload,\nwhich made every blog post creation linear in the number of stored posts.\nexperiments/csharp_objects_profile measures it per tree type and\nexperiments/csharp_tree_delete shows why links are deleted with the resetting\nPlatform.Data.Doublets overload.\n\n== 40e676b\nReport script: README sections in the category/language/bits/size hierarchy\n\nOne JSON report per (category, language, bits, size); Doublets are compared\nwith SQLite of the same durability, and overlapping ranges or medians within\n5% are reported as the same.\n\n== 105f9a6\nLess default work for objects: one blog post takes hundreds of links\n\nRepetitions are work / size clamped to 1..=10; objects now use 500,000 posts of\nwork (5 repetitions at 100,000 posts, 1 at 1,000,000), so that the slowest\nC# objects table still fits a 6 hour CI job.\n\n== 4d83c84\nCI: stable Rust and .NET 10 checks, benchmark matrix that publishes README results; dependabot for cargo and actions\n\n== 48d7fa0\nREADME: methodology, local runs, notes and one generated results section; compare interquartile ranges",
